# Fhenix contracts (Cursor)

When editing Solidity that imports `@fhenixprotocol/cofhe-contracts/FHE.sol` or uses `euint*` / `ebool` / `eaddress`:

1. Never branch on encrypted values with `if` / `require` / `assert` on `ebool` — use `FHE.select`.
2. After every encrypted storage write, call the ACL cascade (`FHE.allowThis`, then `FHE.allowSender` / `FHE.allow` as needed).
3. Prefer bit-shifts over encrypted `mul` / `div` when a power-of-two ratio works.
4. Treat trivial encrypts and event emissions of ciphertexts as plaintext leakage risks.

For full decision trees and lookup recipes, read:

- `plugins/fhenix-toolkit/skills/fhenix-contracts/SKILL.md`
- `plugins/fhenix-toolkit/skills/fhenix-contracts/references/`
